.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt SERVICED 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm serviced
.Nd service manifest format for 5BSD
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Service manifests are UCL files that declare one service each.
They are typically embedded in capability bundles under
.Pa etc/
and parsed by
.Xr libcapbundle 3 .
A maximum of 64 services may be loaded at any time.
.Pp
Labels must be globally unique across all manifests.
Labels and capability names should use reverse-domain format
(containing at least one dot) for the naming registry.
.Ss Required Keys
.Bl -tag -width "program"
.It Va label
Unique service identifier (e.g.,
.Dq org.5bsd.sshd ) .
Maximum 63 characters.
Used in log messages, dependency references, the naming registry,
and control socket responses.
.It Va program
Absolute path to the service executable.
The file must exist and be executable.
.El
.Ss Optional Keys
.Bl -tag -width "max_failures"
.It Va description
Human-readable description of the service.
Cosmetic only.
.It Va user
Drop privileges to this user before executing the service.
The user is resolved via
.Xr getpwnam 3
and supplementary groups via
.Xr getgrouplist 3
at exec time.
If the user does not exist when the service is launched, the
service fails to start and the error is logged.
.It Va group
Drop privileges to this primary group.
Overrides the group obtained from
.Va user
if both are specified.
If the group does not exist at launch time, the service fails to start.
.It Va restart
Restart policy when the service exits.
One of:
.Bl -tag -width "on-failure" -compact
.It Dq never
Do not restart the service.
This is the default.
.It Dq always
Restart unconditionally after exit.
.It Dq on-failure
Restart only on non-zero exit status or signal death.
.El
.It Va stop_timeout
Seconds to wait after sending
.Dv SIGTERM
before escalating to
.Dv SIGKILL .
Clamped to the range 1\(en300.
Default: 5.
.It Va max_failures
Circuit breaker threshold.
After this many consecutive rapid failures, the service is permanently
disabled until the next manifest reload.
Clamped to the range 1\(en100.
Default: 10.
.It Va provides
Array of capability names this service exports.
Maximum 8 entries.
Names must be unique across all loaded manifests; duplicate
.Va provides
names cause the manifest reload to be rejected.
.It Va requires
Array of capability names this service depends on.
Maximum 8 entries.
The service will not start until all required capabilities are
available.
.It Va on_demand
Boolean.
If true, the service is not started during initial launch but instead
launched on first
.Xr service_lookup 3
request for one of its provided names.
Default: false.
.It Va capabilities
Object containing capability tokens to delegate to the service.
See
.Sx Capabilities
below.
.It Va jail
Object describing a jail to create for the service at launch time.
See
.Sx Jail
below.
.El
.Ss Capabilities
The
.Va capabilities
object requests capability tokens from
.Xr oracled 8
on behalf of the service.
Resources listed here that are not pre-declared in
.Xr oracled.conf 5
are automatically claimed by the oracle at runtime.
These
.Em dynamic claims
are reference-counted across all services; when the last service
using a dynamic claim exits, the claim is released from the kernel.
Resources that are declared in
.Xr oracled.conf 5
are
.Em policy claims
and are never released.
.Pp
It may contain the following sub-keys:
.Bl -tag -width "network"
.It Va paths
Array of absolute filesystem paths (maximum 16).
.Xr serviced 8
requests an isolation access token from the oracle for each path
and passes it to the service at launch.
.It Va files
Array of fine-grained file capability objects (maximum 16).
Each object contains:
.Bl -tag -width "actions" -compact
.It Va path
Absolute path to the target file.
Required.
.It Va actions
A string, array of strings, or
.Dq * .
Individual action names are:
.Dq read ,
.Dq write ,
.Dq exec ,
.Dq create ,
.Dq delete ,
.Dq stat ,
.Dq lookup ,
.Dq append ,
.Dq rename_from ,
.Dq rename_to ,
.Dq link ,
.Dq setattr ,
.Dq truncate ,
and
.Dq connect .
The special values
.Dq *
and
.Dq all
grant all actions.
.El
.It Va network
Array of network endpoint capability objects (maximum 16).
Each object contains:
.Bl -tag -width "direction" -compact
.It Va domain
Address family:
.Dq inet
(default),
.Dq inet6 ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va protocol
Transport protocol:
.Dq tcp ,
.Dq udp ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va port
Integer port number, or
.Dq * .
.It Va ports
Port range as a string
.Dq min-max ,
or
.Dq * .
Only one of
.Va port
or
.Va ports
should be specified.
.It Va direction
.Dq bind
(default),
.Dq connect ,
or
.Dq * .
.It Va address
IP address or CIDR notation (e.g.,
.Dq 10.0.0.0/24 ) .
Optional.
.It Va prefix
CIDR prefix length as an integer.
Optional; provides an alternative to embedding the prefix in
.Va address .
.El
.It Va jails
Array of jail operation tokens (maximum 16).
Grants the service authority to perform jail operations via
delegated capability tokens.
.It Va system
Array of system gate names (maximum 16).
.Xr serviced 8
requests a system access token from the oracle with the specified
gates and passes it to the service.
See
.Xr mac_capability_system 4
for the list of available gate names.
.El
.Ss Jail
The optional
.Va jail
object creates a jail for the service at launch time.
It contains the following keys:
.Bl -tag -width "hostname"
.It Va name Pq required
Jail name.
.It Va path Pq required
Root filesystem path for the jail.
.It Va hostname
Hostname inside the jail.
Defaults to the value of
.Va name .
.It Va ip4
IPv4 address to assign to the jail.
.El
.Ss Dependency Resolution
Before launching services,
.Xr serviced 8
topologically sorts all loaded manifests by their
.Va provides
and
.Va requires
declarations.
Services that provide capabilities are started before services
that require them.
.Pp
The following rules apply:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Dq ORACLED
is an implicit provider that is always satisfied.
Services may list it in
.Va requires
without a corresponding
.Va provides .
.It
Unknown providers (those not declared by any loaded manifest) produce
a warning but are treated as satisfied.
.It
Dependency cycles are fatal: no services are started if a cycle is
detected.
.It
Duplicate
.Va label
values or duplicate
.Va provides
names across manifests cause the entire reload to be rejected.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Minimal service manifest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# myservice.ucl
label = "myservice";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/myservice";
restart = "always";
.Ed
.Pp
Service with dependencies and file capabilities:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
label = "org.5bsd.webapp";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/webapp";
description = "Example web application";
user = "www";
group = "www";
provides = ["http"];
requires = ["database"];
restart = "on-failure";
stop_timeout = 10;
max_failures = 20;
capabilities {
    paths = ["/var/www"];
    files = [
        {
            path = "/var/log/webapp.log";
            actions = ["write", "create", "append"];
        },
    ];
    network = [
        {
            port = 8080;
            protocol = "tcp";
            direction = "bind";
            address = "127.0.0.1";
        },
        {
            domain = "inet";
            protocol = "tcp";
            direction = "connect";
            address = "10.0.0.0/24";
            ports = "5432-5433";
        },
    ];
    system = ["sysctl"];
}
.Ed
.Pp
Service running inside a jail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
label = "org.5bsd.sandboxed";
program = "/usr/local/sbin/sandboxed";
restart = "on-failure";
jail {
    name = "sandboxed";
    path = "/var/jails/sandboxed";
    hostname = "sandboxed.local";
    ip4 = "10.0.0.2";
}
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/Capabilities/System/"
.It Pa /Capabilities/System/
System capability bundles.
Each
.Pa *.cap
directory may contain Service.ucl files in the same format;
see
.Xr libcapbundle 3 .
.It Pa /Capabilities/
User-installed capability bundles.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libcapbundle 3 ,
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr mac_capability_isolation 4 ,
.Xr mac_capability_system 4 ,
.Xr oracled.conf 5 ,
.Xr oracled 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8 ,
.Xr servicectl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
manifest format first appeared in 5BSD.
